HeliBoard
  Copyright Helium314 and contributors
  https://github.com/HeliBorg/HeliBoard
  GNU General Public License v3.0
  This keyboard is a modified HeliBoard. The big button performs the field's declared
  editor action even when the field sets IME_FLAG_NO_ENTER_ACTION, which is the approach
  discussed in HeliBoard issue 1989 (Pixel launcher and browser search fields).
  The 123 and #+= pages use HeliBoard's JSON layout format (itself from FlorisBoard)
  for the iOS US symbol rows. The arrangement follows the iOS layout shared in
  HeliBoard discussion 2180.
  A short tap tries the field's editor action, then the enter key. Flutter's input
  connection returns true from performEditorAction and drops the action; the text
  is checked afterwards, and the enter key, DPAD center, and numpad enter follow
  when it did not change. FlorisBoard moves the caret with DPAD key events when
  setSelection cannot be trusted. An index outside the text is not sent, because
  editors clamp that index to the end of the field.
  The mic becomes Send from the composing text, the committed text, or a direct
  read of the field. AOSP LatinIME keeps that text in the connection cache. Search
  fields and Compose report no selection, so the cache is not the only source.
  TextView sets IME_FLAG_NO_ENTER_ACTION on a multiline field, and HeliBoard then
  draws a return key (issue 1989). The big button stays Send. FlorisBoard commits a
  newline for an unspecified action, which does not deliver a key event (issue 3262).
  A field with no action gets KEYCODE_ENTER instead of that newline.

OpenBoard and the Android Open Source LatinIME
  Copyright The Android Open Source Project
  Apache License 2.0
  Cursor movement uses InputConnection.setSelection, and an unknown selection (-1) is
  not a cursor position (Constants.NOT_A_CURSOR_POSITION). When setSelection fails, the
  caret is moved with DPAD key events, the same fallback AOSP uses when the editor
  connection cannot be read.

FlorisBoard
  Copyright Patrick Goldinger and contributors
  https://github.com/florisboard/florisboard
  Apache License 2.0
  FlorisBoard pull request 1822 keeps a local editor cache when a selection callback is
  not a real move, instead of re-reading the field. Space-bar cursor swipes there send
  DPAD key events (see the FlorisBoard touch-gesture docs). Both are used here when a
  WebView, browser, or React Native field (including X compose and reply) drops or
  ignores the selection. No FlorisBoard source file was copied.

